course: dictionary
lesson: 8239
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Rewire» is one of these words. In its first meaning, you put new electrical wires into a machine, lamp or building. The prefix re- means again or back, so to rewire is to wire something again in a new way.
explain: «Old houses need rewiring for safety.» The clues are old houses and safety, so the wires are being replaced to keep people safe. Electricity is dangerous, so rewiring is a job for a qualified electrician, never for children.
explain: The second meaning is informal, and you will hear it in talk about learning. «The brain keeps rewiring until about 25.» Here the brain does not get real wires. It changes how it works through practice. Wires and circuits point to the first meaning, while brains, habits and practice point to the second.
fact: Rewire means to put new electrical wires into something, or to connect them in a new way.
fact: In informal talk, rewire can mean to change how you think or act through practice.
fact: The prefix re- means again or back, so rewire means to wire again.
fact: Mains electricity can kill, so never touch wires or plugs. Only a qualified electrician should rewire a house.
fact: A quick check: if the sentence is about bulbs, switches or houses, it means the first meaning. If it is about learning, brains or habits, it means the second.
exercise: «Old houses need rewiring for safety.» What does rewiring mean here? | Painting the walls a new colour | Moving the furniture around | Cleaning the windows | *Putting new electrical wires into the house
exercise: «The brain keeps rewiring until about 25.» What does rewiring mean here? | Sleeping for a long time | Cutting the brain into small pieces | *Changing how the brain works, through learning and practice | Putting new wires inside your head
exercise: Jayden wants to rewire the lamp in his bedroom. What should he do? | Rewire it himself, because children can do this safely | *Ask a qualified electrician, because mains electricity can kill | Rewire it quickly while it is still plugged in | Ask his little sister to hold the wires
test: «Many blind people use sounds more skilfully, partly because the brain rewires.» What does rewires mean here? | Breaks into small pieces | *Changes how it works through practice | Makes a loud noise | Runs faster when you are asleep
test: In a science lesson, pupils rewire a simple circuit to add a switch. What does rewire mean? | Wrap the wires in paper | Draw a picture of the circuit | *Connect the wires in a new way | Turn the bulb off with your hands
exam: The prefix re- in rewire means: | *Again | Under | Without | Far away
